-          "quote": "Assume AC, let $h>0$ and $x,y\\in\\mathbb R$, and let $\\mu_{x,y}^h$ be the\nlaw on $C([0,h])$ of the bridge in\n[[def-scalar-brownian-bridge-from-x-to-y]]. If $X_s=x+W_s$ is Brownian motion\nstarted at $x$, then for every Borel path event $A\\subseteq C([0,h])$ and\nBorel set $D\\subseteq\\mathbb R$,\n$$\\mathbb P\\{X\\in A,\\ X_h\\in D\\}=\n\\int_D p_h(y-x)\\,\\mu_{x,y}^h(A)\\,dy,$$\nwhere $p_t(z)=(2\\pi t)^{-1/2}e^{-z^2/(2t)}$. In particular this specifies\nthe endpoint-conditioned bridge law for every endpoint $y$. For every\n$0\\le t<h$, the restriction of $\\mu_{x,y}^h$ to path events up to time $t$\nhas density\n$$\\frac{p_{h-t}(y-X_t)}{p_h(y-x)}$$\nrelative to Brownian motion $X$ started at $x$ on $[0,t]$.",
+          "quote": "Assume AC, let $h>0$ and $x,y\\in\\mathbb R$, and let $\\mu_{x,y}^h$ be the\nlaw on $C([0,h])$ of the bridge in\n[[def-scalar-brownian-bridge-from-x-to-y]]. If $X_s=x+W_s$ is Brownian motion\nstarted at $x$, then for every Borel path event $A\\subseteq C([0,h])$ and\nBorel set $D\\subseteq\\mathbb R$,\n$$\\mathbb P\\{X\\in A,\\ X_h\\in D\\}= \\int_D p_h(y-x)\\,\\mu_{x,y}^h(A)\\,dy,$$\nwhere $p_t(z)=(2\\pi t)^{-1/2}e^{-z^2/(2t)}$. In particular this specifies\nthe endpoint-conditioned bridge law for every endpoint $y$. For every\n$0\\le t<h$, the restriction of $\\mu_{x,y}^h$ to path events up to time $t$\nhas density\n$$\\frac{p_{h-t}(y-X_t)}{p_h(y-x)}$$\nrelative to Brownian motion $X$ started at $x$ on $[0,t]$.",
